{"term":"aspect","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:fbcc495529a7ec7877","definition":"Any specific feature, part, or element of something.","example":"Japan's aging population is an important aspect of its economy.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["component","facet","feature"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["aspectism","aspective","aspectless","aspect particle","aspect ratio","aspect-related","aspectual","in full aspect","in trian aspect","modified aspect ratio","multiaspect","multi-aspect","multiple-aspect","original aspect ratio"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/aspect#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:5f31070fe8c0b00b61","definition":"The way something appears when viewed from a certain direction or perspective.","example":"The stone has a greenish aspect in this light.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["hue"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["aspectism","aspective","aspectless","aspect particle","aspect ratio","aspect-related","aspectual","in full aspect","in trian aspect","modified aspect ratio","multiaspect","multi-aspect","multiple-aspect","original aspect ratio"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/aspect#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:a58c5680305e821cac","definition":"The way something appears when considered from a certain point of view.","example":"in certain aspects [ = in certain respects]","pos":"noun","synonyms":["respect","front"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["aspectism","aspective","aspectless","aspect particle","aspect ratio","aspect-related","aspectual","in full aspect","in trian aspect","modified aspect ratio","multiaspect","multi-aspect","multiple-aspect","original aspect ratio"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/aspect#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:689fc0faf942ae00ea","definition":"A phase or a partial, but significant view or description of something.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["aspectism","aspective","aspectless","aspect particle","aspect ratio","aspect-related","aspectual","in full aspect","in trian aspect","modified aspect ratio","multiaspect","multi-aspect","multiple-aspect","original aspect ratio"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/aspect#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:807dad152f91b933c5","definition":"One's appearance or expression.","example":"Art thou but Captaine of a thouſand horſe,\nThat by Characters grauen in thy browes,\nAnd by thy martiall face and ſtout aſpect,\nDeſeru’ſt to haue the leading of an hoſte?","pos":"noun","synonyms":["appearance","look","blee"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["aspectism","aspective","aspectless","aspect particle","aspect ratio","aspect-related","aspectual","in full aspect","in trian aspect","modified aspect ratio","multiaspect","multi-aspect","multiple-aspect","original aspect ratio"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/aspect#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:f9792eb742f1de9f63","definition":"Position or situation with regard to seeing; that position which enables one to look in a particular direction; position in relation to the points of the compass.","example":"The house has a southern aspect, i.e. a position which faces the south.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["aspectism","aspective","aspectless","aspect particle","aspect ratio","aspect-related","aspectual","in full aspect","in trian aspect","modified aspect ratio","multiaspect","multi-aspect","multiple-aspect","original aspect ratio"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/aspect#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:2126f47660ad354a50","definition":"Prospect; outlook.","example":"This town affords a good aspect toward the hill from whence we descended ; nor does it deceive us ; for it is handsomely built […]","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["aspectism","aspective","aspectless","aspect particle","aspect ratio","aspect-related","aspectual","in full aspect","in trian aspect","modified aspect ratio","multiaspect","multi-aspect","multiple-aspect","original aspect ratio"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/aspect#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:20a1d80fe54fea2808","definition":"A grammatical quality of a verb which determines the relationship of the speaker to the internal temporal flow of the event which the verb describes, or whether the speaker views the event from outside as a whole, or from within as it is unfolding.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["aspectism","aspective","aspectless","aspect particle","aspect ratio","aspect-related","aspectual","in full aspect","in trian aspect","modified aspect ratio","multiaspect","multi-aspect","multiple-aspect","original aspect ratio"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/aspect#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:a12e74ad509e109c79","definition":"The relative position of heavenly bodies as they appear to an observer on earth; the angular relationship between points in a horoscope.","example":"[…] To the blanc moon / Her office they prescribed; to the other five / Their planetary motions, and aspects, / In sextile, square, and trine, and opposite, / Of noxious efficacy, and when to join / In synod unbenign; and taught the fix'd / their influence malignant when to shower, / Which of them rising with the sun, or falling / Should prove tempestuous: […]","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["aspectism","aspective","aspectless","aspect particle","aspect ratio","aspect-related","aspectual","in full aspect","in trian aspect","modified aspect ratio","multiaspect","multi-aspect","multiple-aspect","original aspect ratio"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/aspect#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:73b8f9ea302bf49f13","definition":"The personified manifestation of a deity that represents one or more of its characteristics or functions.","example":"The Mother Goddess in her many manifestations is termed Shakti, the female energy in creation, and worshipped as the supreme female aspect of Brahman.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["aspectism","aspective","aspectless","aspect particle","aspect ratio","aspect-related","aspectual","in full aspect","in trian aspect","modified aspect ratio","multiaspect","multi-aspect","multiple-aspect","original aspect ratio"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/aspect#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:5f039b72d3203b6ecd","definition":"The act of looking at something; gaze.","example":"The tradition is no less ancient, that the basilisk killeth by aspect ; and that the wolf, if he see a man first, by aspect striketh a man hoarse.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"obsolete","wordFamily":["aspectism","aspective","aspectless","aspect particle","aspect ratio","aspect-related","aspectual","in full aspect","in trian aspect","modified aspect ratio","multiaspect","multi-aspect","multiple-aspect","original aspect ratio"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/aspect#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:60246259e200d19b0b","definition":"Appearance to the eye or the mind; look; view.","example":"1684-1690, Thomas Burnet, Sacred Theory of the Earth Vol 1, Chapter IX.\nThey are both in my judgment the image or picture of a great Ruine, and have the true aspect of a World lying in its rubbish.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"obsolete","wordFamily":["aspectism","aspective","aspectless","aspect particle","aspect ratio","aspect-related","aspectual","in full aspect","in trian aspect","modified aspect ratio","multiaspect","multi-aspect","multiple-aspect","original aspect ratio"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/aspect#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:94781f09e8bdc363be","definition":"In aspect-oriented programming, a feature or component that can be applied to parts of a program independent of any inheritance hierarchy.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["aspectism","aspective","aspectless","aspect particle","aspect ratio","aspect-related","aspectual","in full aspect","in trian aspect","modified aspect ratio","multiaspect","multi-aspect","multiple-aspect","original aspect ratio"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/aspect#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:7a1e24bca714e8fc9d","definition":"The visual indication of railway signal as displayed to the driver. With three-aspect colour light signals this would be red, yellow or green, and on four-aspect signals, double-yellow also; a two-aspect signal displays red or green.","example":"It was in this work [on the Southern Railway] that the four-aspect system of indications, using red, yellow, double yellow, and green, was first installed. […][page 229, photo caption] Three-aspect colour-light signal with three-way junction indicator, Bow Junction, Eastern Region","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["aspectism","aspective","aspectless","aspect particle","aspect ratio","aspect-related","aspectual","in full aspect","in trian aspect","modified aspect ratio","multiaspect","multi-aspect","multiple-aspect","original aspect ratio"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/aspect#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:f6b0fce077abbdd5aa","definition":"To have a particular aspect or type of aspect.","example":"","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["aspectism","aspective","aspectless","aspect particle","aspect ratio","aspect-related","aspectual","in full aspect","in trian aspect","modified aspect ratio","multiaspect","multi-aspect","multiple-aspect","original aspect ratio"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/aspect#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:08cf07e8fe8224584c","definition":"To channel a divine being.","example":"","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordF